<!--
    De-vectorized reduction, `option devectorize on|off`. Same witness as
    kuna-wideslice.xml: clang -O3 x86-64 byte_sum, eight bytes per iteration
    widened through SSE unpacks into eight dword lane accumulators, folded after
    the loop, with a scalar remainder loop.

    Pass 1 (default, option off): the compiler's shape: the `8 <= length` guard,
    eight lane accumulators, the fold and the second loop. Pass 2 (`option
    devectorize on`): the guard's vector edge is removed and the function is the
    source loop, `v1 += bytes[v2]` over every byte.

    This self-contained byte_sum regression embeds 143 bytes of x86-64 code
    loaded at 0x1000.
-->
